  "type": "people",
  "content": "<div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/2/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></a> <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">3</span></span> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/4/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">4</span></a></div><p>Although she and Harrison were a close couple, Pattie was rarely present in the studio while The Beatles were recording.</p><blockquote><div>It was one of those flat cap attitudes which we were losing by then. I think if <a href=\"/people/maureen-starkey/\">Maureen</a> came to the studio five or six times that would be about it, and in all the years Pattie came several times at most. I don&#8217;t remember <a href=\"/people/cynthia-lennon/\">Cynthia</a> coming much when she was married to John. It was just something that didn&#8217;t happen.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Ringo Starr<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>Despite this, she appeared on a number of Beatles songs. Pattie participated in the chorus of <a href=\"/songs/yellow-submarine/\">&#8216;Yellow Submarine&#8217;</a>, recorded at Abbey Road on <a href=\"/1966/06/01/recording-yellow-submarine-2/\">1 June 1966</a>, and helped out on the song&#8217;s various special effects.</p><p>She was also present for the <a href=\"/1967/02/10/recording-a-day-in-the-life-4/\">10 February 1967</a> orchestral overdubs for <a href=\"/songs/a-day-in-the-life/\">&#8216;A Day In The Life&#8217;</a>, which were filmed for a mooted television special but never shown. And on 25 June she sat cross-legged on the studio floor as The Beatles performed &#8216;All You Need Is Love&#8217; for the <a href=\"/1967/06/25/the-beatles-on-our-world-all-you-need-is-love/\"><em>Our World</em> satellite link-up</a>; also present were Mick Jagger, Marianne Faithfull, Keith Richard, Eric Clapton, Keith Moon and <a href=\"/people/jane-asher/\">Jane Asher</a>.</p><div class=\"epyt-video-wrapper\"><iframe  id=\"_ytid_11392\"  width=\"580\" height=\"326\"  data-origwidth=\"580\" data-origheight=\"326\"  data-relstop=\"1\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/usNsCeOV4GM?enablejsapi=1&#038;autoplay=0&#038;cc_load_policy=0&#038;cc_lang_pref=&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;loop=0&#038;rel=0&#038;fs=1&#038;playsinline=0&#038;autohide=2&#038;theme=dark&#038;color=red&#038;controls=1&#038;disablekb=0&#038;\" class=\"__youtube_prefs__  epyt-is-override  no-lazyload\" title=\"YouTube player\"  allow=\"fullscreen; accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen data-no-lazy=\"1\" data-skipgform_ajax_framebjll=\"\"></iframe></div><p>Perhaps the song most prominently featuring Pattie was <a href=\"/songs/birthday/\">&#8216;Birthday&#8217;</a> on the <a href=\"/albums/the-beatles-white-album/\">White Album</a>; she performed backing vocals on the song with <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a>\u2019s then-girlfriend <a href=\"/people/yoko-ono/\">Yoko Ono</a>.</p><p>Although George Harrison later downplayed the connection, saying he envisaged it being sung by Ray Charles, it is widely held that he wrote <a href=\"/songs/something/\">&#8216;Something&#8217;</a>, one of <a href=\"/albums/abbey-road/\">Abbey Road</a>\u2019s highlights, for Pattie.</p><blockquote><div>He told me in a matter-of-fact way that he had written it for me. I thought it was beautiful and it turned out to be the most successful song he ever wrote, with more than 150 cover versions.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Pattie Boyd<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/pattie-boyd-wonderful\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Wonderful Today</em></a></div><p>Pattie and George Harrison were arrested on <a href=\"/1969/03/12/george-pattie-harrison-drugs-squad-raid/\">12 March 1969</a> at their Esher home for possession of marijuana, following a police raid. It took place on the day of Paul McCartney&#8217;s wedding to Linda Eastman.</p><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/&quot;}' id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-421 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/690312-george-harrison_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTM5IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEzOSI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"139\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690312-george-harrison_01-200x139.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison, Kinfauns, 12 March 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690312-george-harrison_01-200x139.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690312-george-harrison_01-580x403.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690312-george-harrison_01-960x667.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690312-george-harrison_01-768x533.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690312-george-harrison_01.jpg 1024w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"28156\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/690312-george-harrison_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690312-george-harrison_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1024,711\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison, Kinfauns, 12 March 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690312-george-harrison_01-960x667.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/george-harrison/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTYxIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE2MSI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"161\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01-200x161.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George and Pattie Harrison, 18 March 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01-200x161.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01-580x466.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01-960x771.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01-768x617.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01.jpg 1393w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"28261\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/george-harrison/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1393,1119\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George and Pattie Harrison, 18 March 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690318-george-pattie-harrison_01-960x771.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/03/31/george-pattie-harrison-fined-drugs-possession/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTU0IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE1NCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"154\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01-200x154.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George and Pattie Harrison outside Esher and Walton Magistrates&#039; Court, 31 March 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01-200x154.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01-580x448.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01-960x742.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01-768x593.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01.jpg 1024w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"28550\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/03/31/george-pattie-harrison-fined-drugs-possession/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1024,791\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George and Pattie Harrison outside Esher and Walton Magistrates&amp;#8217; Court, 31 March 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690331-george-pattie-harrison_01-960x742.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/68_george-pattie-harrison_001/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNTkiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTU5IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"159\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_george-pattie-harrison_001-159x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George and Pattie Harrison, 31 March 1969\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_george-pattie-harrison_001-159x200.jpg 159w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_george-pattie-harrison_001-460x580.jpg 460w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_george-pattie-harrison_001.jpg 570w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 159px) 100vw, 159px\" data-attachment-id=\"8514\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/68_george-pattie-harrison_001/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_george-pattie-harrison_001.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"570,719\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George and Pattie Harrison, 31 March 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/68_george-pattie-harrison_001.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><blockquote><div>I was with George in the office when that call came through. It was the end of a long day at Apple. Pattie rang and said, &#8216;They&#8217;re here \u2013 the law is here,&#8217; and we knew what to do by then. We phoned Release&#8217;s lawyer, Martin Polden. We had a routine: he came round to Apple, and we all went down by limousine to Esher, where the police were well ensconced by then \u2013 and I stood bail for George and Pattie. They went off to the police station.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Derek Taylor<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>Pattie&#8217;s relationship with George began to decline after The Beatles&#8217; trip to India in early 1968.</p><blockquote><div>George had become obsessive about meditation. He was also sometimes withdrawn and depressed.</p><p>My moods started to mirror his and at times I felt almost suicidal. I don&#8217;t think I was ever in any real danger of killing myself but I got as far as working out how I would do it: put on a diaphanous Ossie Clark dress and throw myself off Beachy Head.</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Pattie Boyd<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/pattie-boyd-wonderful\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Wonderful Today</em></a></div><p>In March 1970, George and Pattie Harrison moved into a new house \u2013 Friar Park, a Victorian Gothic mansion near Henley-on-Thames, Oxfordshire.</p><blockquote><div>That whole period was insane. Friar Park was a madhouse. Our lives were fuelled by alcohol and cocaine, and so it was with everyone who came into our sphere. We were all as drunk, stoned and single-minded as each other. Nobody seemed to have appointments, deadlines or anything pressing in their lives, no structure and no responsibilities.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Pattie Boyd<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/pattie-boyd-wonderful\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Wonderful Today</em></a></div><p>George&#8217;s attentions often wandered to other women, and Pattie knew that he was unfaithful to her \u2013 most notably with Ringo Starr&#8217;s wife <a href=\"/people/maureen-starkey/\">Maureen</a>.</p><blockquote><div>She was the last person I would have expected to stab me in the back. I discovered from some photos that she had been staying in the house with George while I had visited my mother in Devon. He had given her a beautiful necklace, which she wore in front of me.</p><p>Then I found them locked in a bedroom at Friar Park. I stood outside banging on the door yelling: &#8216;What are you doing? Maureen&#8217;s in there, isn&#8217;t she? I know she is!&#8217; George just laughed.</p><p>Eventually he opened the door and said: &#8216;Oh, she&#8217;s just a bit tired so she&#8217;s lying down.&#8217;</p><p>I went straight to the top of the house and lowered the flag bearing the om symbol that George had been flying from the roof and hoisted a skull and crossbones instead. That made me feel much better.</p><p>Maureen wasn&#8217;t even prepared to be subtle. She would turn up at Friar Park at midnight and I would say: &#8216;What the hell are you doing here?&#8217; &#8216;I&#8217;ve come to listen to George playing in the studio.&#8217; &#8216;Well, I&#8217;m going to bed.&#8217; &#8216;Ah, well, I&#8217;m going to the studio.&#8217;</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Pattie Boyd<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/pattie-boyd-wonderful\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Wonderful Today</em></a></div><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/2/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></a> <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">3</span></span> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/pattie-boyd/4/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">4</span></a></div>",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-10-25"
